            <ArticleTitle>[Thrombocyte aggregating capacity in ischemic heart disease caused by coronary arteriosclerosis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>49-53</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A distinct increase in the aggregative property of blood platelets, displayed by an increased degree of aggregation and enlargement of the platelet aggregates, was revealed in patients with ischemic disease of the heart. The more severe the atherosclerotic process in the coronary arteries (according to the findings of selective coronarography), the more is the aggregative property of platelets intensified. The stimulating effect of smoking on platelet aggregation was also established.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
